import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Section Formula & Mid-Point Formula | Coordinate Geometry | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn the Section Formula for internal division in ratio m1:m2, Mid-point formula, and the k:1 ratio technique for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/coordinate-geometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Coordinate Geometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">02</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Section Formula & <span>Mid-Point Formula</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master internal division of line segments in ratio m₁:m₂, the mid-point formula, and finding ratios using the k:1 trick.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THE SECTION FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · SECTION FORMULA</div>
					<h2>Internal Division in Ratio m₁ : m₂</h2>
					<p>
						The coordinates of point <strong>P(x, y)</strong> which divides the line segment joining <strong>A(x₁, y₁)</strong> and <strong>B(x₂, y₂)</strong> internally in the ratio <strong>m₁ : m₂</strong> are:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>P(x, y) = ( (m₁x₂ + m₂x₁) / (m₁ + m₂), (m₁y₂ + m₂y₁) / (m₁ + m₂) )</strong>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>The k : 1 Ratio Trick</strong>
							<p>
								When finding the ratio in which point <em>P</em> divides line segment <em>AB</em>, assume the ratio to be <strong>k : 1</strong>. The coordinates become:
								<br/>
								<strong>P(x, y) = ( (kx₂ + x₁) / (k + 1), (ky₂ + y₁) / (k + 1) )</strong>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · MID-POINT FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · MID-POINT FORMULA</div>
					<h2>Mid-Point of a Line Segment</h2>
					<p>
						If <em>P</em> is the <strong>mid-point</strong> of line segment <em>AB</em>, the ratio is <strong>1 : 1</strong> (m₁ = 1, m₂ = 1). The formula simplifies to:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>Mid-Point M = ( (x₁ + x₂) / 2, (y₁ + y₂) / 2 )</strong>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find coordinates of point P dividing A(4, -3) and B(8, 5) in ratio 3 : 1</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given: x₁ = 4, y₁ = -3, x₂ = 8, y₂ = 5, m₁ = 3, m₂ = 1.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x = (3 × 8 + 1 × 4) / (3 + 1) = (24 + 4) / 4 = 28/4 = <strong>7</strong><br/>
								y = (3 × 5 + 1 × (-3)) / (3 + 1) = (15 - 3) / 4 = 12/4 = <strong>3</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Coordinates of P are <strong>(7, 3)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Find the ratio in which Y-axis divides A(-4, 2) and B(3, -5)</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Since the point lies on the <strong>Y-axis</strong>, its x-coordinate is <strong>0</strong>. Let ratio = k : 1.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x = (k(3) + 1(-4)) / (k + 1) = 0<br/>
								3k - 4 = 0 ⟹ <strong>k = 4/3</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">The Y-axis divides line segment AB in the ratio <strong>4 : 3</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Section formula coordinates: <strong>( (m₁x₂ + m₂x₁)/(m₁+m₂), (m₁y₂ + m₂y₁)/(m₁+m₂) )</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Mid-point formula: <strong>( (x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2 )</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Point on X-axis has coordinates <strong>(x, 0)</strong>; point on Y-axis has coordinates <strong>(0, y)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/coordinate-geometry/distance-formula" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Distance Formula</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/coordinate-geometry/applications-and-practice" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Trisection & Practice</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

